title: The Shadow Cabinet
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: shadow_cabinet_timer <= 0 and con_in_government = 0
on-arrival: shadow_cabinet_timer = 4; month_actions += 1

= The Shadow Cabinet

Your front bench is a coalition. Most of its members served under Heath, and a good number of them think the party made a mistake in 1975.

- @dries: Promote the dries.
- @balance: Keep the wets in the big jobs.
- @heath_offer: Offer Edward Heath a way back.
- @heath_freeze: Freeze Heath out.
- @whips: Let the whips loose.
- @easy_discard

@dries
subtitle: Dries strengthen; wets resent it.
on-arrival: dry_strength += 5; dry_dissent -= 5; wet_dissent += 6; wet_strength -= 2

Young believers in the market get front-bench jobs. Several Heathites read it as a purge in slow motion.

@balance
subtitle: Calms the wets, frustrates the dries.
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 6; dry_dissent += 4

The economic portfolios stay balanced. Keith Joseph complains that you will never change the country with a cabinet that doesn't want to change it.

@heath_offer
view-if: heath_hostility >= 30
subtitle: Heath is unlikely to accept, but the gesture matters.
on-arrival: heath_hostility -= 12; wet_dissent -= 4; dry_dissent += 4; right_dissent += 2; thatcher_rating -= 1

You let it be known that Heath would be welcome in a future government. He doesn't reply, but the wets notice that you asked.

@heath_freeze
subtitle: The dries cheer; the feud deepens.
on-arrival: heath_hostility += 10; dry_dissent -= 3; wet_dissent += 3

Heath gets no briefings, no invitations and no role. He makes sure the press hears how he feels about it.

@whips
subtitle: -1 resource. Lowers dissent in every faction.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires 1 resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; dry_dissent -= 3; wet_dissent -= 3; loyalist_dissent -= 3; right_dissent -= 3

Humphrey Atkins and his whips remind colleagues, gently and less gently, where their careers come from.
